Subject: [PATCH 3/3] match.TIEBREAK_REGEN = client16402_stops_after_end: the
 elixir regen stops after the step into t6003 under the drain

Mechanic: phase_upkeep regenerated elixir on past a level overtime's end. Under OVERTIME_TIEBREAK = client_hp_drain no play is
accepted from that end (tiebreak_frozen), and the live bar stops too: its last step is the one into t6003 (end + 150 ms). New arm
client16402_stops_after_end (shipped; TIEBREAK_REGEN_STOP_MS = 150); old arm runs; format-3 snapshots keep it. No play effect
(nothing can be played then); the bar is what a player and the model observe.

Minimal reproduction: tests/tiebreak_regen.rs: a battle with no play put on t5990, bars emptied: regen steps into t5991..t6003,
none after. Plant tiebreak_regen_runs turns it red.

Parity-Evidence: ClashBot scratchpad/gauntlet/L74/parity/fin15 (probe_j4.py; FIN15.md round 3) on client 16.402 live frame logs:
20261018_020557 3.0096 on t6001, 3.117 on t6003 / t6005 / t6007 ...; 20261017_061258 6.6057 on t6001, 6.7131 on t6004 / t6005;
20261017_064045 5.2829 on t6004 / t6006. J4's 3x phase (135 matches) was 0.937 with the regen running on.
